{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"c260f5e618e167cf","name":"card_event_hold_the_line","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/events/card_event_hold_the_line","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HOLD THE LINE","text":"When an enemy unit enters the frontline, pin and deal 1 damage to all units in the frontline.","flavorText":"The German invasion of Poland started on 1 September 1939, and on 17 September the Soviet forces invaded Eastern Poland. Facing overwhelming odds the Polish armed forces managed to resist both nations until early October, or for 5 weeks. The Polish plan against Germany was to delay them as long as possible as they expected France and Britain to come to their aid before the Germans overwhelmed their defenses. However, both Britain and France anticipated that Poland would hold out for 2-3 months, while Polish commanders expected them to hold out for 6 months. On 7 September 1939 the French started an offensive in the Saar region in an attempt to divert German forces from Poland, but their advance soon came to a halt without any significant number of German units being withdrawn. Meanwhile Britain was more focused on naval matters which did not do much to halt the German advance, and on 17 September the Royal Navy lost the aircraft carrier Courageous to a German u boat torpedo, which was a devastating psychological blow. That same day the Soviet Union declared war on Poland and that diminished any hopes that the Western Allies had of saving Poland from falling.","faction":"Poland","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_hold_the_line","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_hold_the_line_title","SourceString":"HOLD THE LINE","LocalizedString":"HOLD THE LINE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_hold_the_line_text","SourceString":"When an enemy unit enters the frontline, pin and deal 1 damage to all units in the frontline.","LocalizedString":"When an enemy unit enters the frontline, pin and deal 1 damage to all units in the frontline."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_hold_the_line_history","SourceString":"The German invasion of Poland started on 1 September 1939, and on 17 September the Soviet forces invaded Eastern Poland. Facing overwhelming odds the Polish armed forces managed to resist both nations until early October, or for 5 weeks. The Polish plan against Germany was to delay them as long as possible as they expected France and Britain to come to their aid before the Germans overwhelmed their defenses. However, both Britain and France anticipated that Poland would hold out for 2-3 months, while Polish commanders expected them to hold out for 6 months. On 7 September 1939 the French started an offensive in the Saar region in an attempt to divert German forces from Poland, but their advance soon came to a halt without any significant number of German units being withdrawn. Meanwhile Britain was more focused on naval matters which did not do much to halt the German advance, and on 17 September the Royal Navy lost the aircraft carrier Courageous to a German u boat torpedo, which was a devastating psychological blow. That same day the Soviet Union declared war on Poland and that diminished any hopes that the Western Allies had of saving Poland from falling.","LocalizedString":"The German invasion of Poland started on 1 September 1939, and on 17 September the Soviet forces invaded Eastern Poland. Facing overwhelming odds the Polish armed forces managed to resist both nations until early October, or for 5 weeks. The Polish plan against Germany was to delay them as long as possible as they expected France and Britain to come to their aid before the Germans overwhelmed their defenses. However, both Britain and France anticipated that Poland would hold out for 2-3 months, while Polish commanders expected them to hold out for 6 months. On 7 September 1939 the French started an offensive in the Saar region in an attempt to divert German forces from Poland, but their advance soon came to a halt without any significant number of German units being withdrawn. Meanwhile Britain was more focused on naval matters which did not do much to halt the German advance, and on 17 September the Royal Navy lost the aircraft carrier Courageous to a German u boat torpedo, which was a devastating psychological blow. That same day the Soviet Union declared war on Poland and that diminished any hopes that the Western Allies had of saving Poland from falling."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardMoveToFrontline"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Poland/t_last_ditch.t_last_ditch","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::Top","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/HOLD_THE_LINE.HOLD_THE_LINE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":401.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_hold_the_line_photo","SourceString":"Polish soldiers with anti-aircraft gun near the Warsaw Central Station, September 1939.","LocalizedString":"Polish soldiers with anti-aircraft gun near the Warsaw Central Station, September 1939."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"Notes":"Image needed to be customized"